"status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://rbwm.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-23","committee":"Place Overview and Scrutiny Panel","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://rbwm.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-29","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://rbwm.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-14","committee":"Adults, Children and Health Overview and Scrutiny Panel","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://rbwm.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-20","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://rbwm.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-09","committee":"Berkshire Pension Board","time":"11.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://rbwm.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-10","committee":"Corporate Overview and Scrutiny Panel","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://rbwm.moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-30","committee":"Council","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed; Extraordinary","webcast":false,"url":"https://rbwm.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-01","committee":"Berkshire Pension Board","time":"11.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://rbwm.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-07","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://rbwm.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-14","committee":"Standing Advisory Council on Religious Education","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://rbwm.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Corporate Overview and Scrutiny Panel","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://rbwm.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Berkshire Pension Fund becomes cash-flow positive but funding stalled at 86%","lead":"The Berkshire Pension Fund moved to cash-flow positive at its 2025 valuation, meaning contributions from members and employers now exceed pension benefit payments, ending the need for council cash injections to finance current pension payments. The fund can therefore focus its investment strategy on long-term capital growth. However, the fund remains 86% funded, unchanged from 2022, with full funding not expected until March 2040. The committee identified two significant emerging risks: the proposed Ridgeway Authority local government reorganisation could result in transfers of members, assets and liabilities between pension funds with unclear wider implications; and workforce resilience concerns, with specialist knowledge concentrated in a small number of officers, raising succession planning risks. Scheme employers face less than a 33% probability of contribution rates exceeding a 35% maximum threshold in the short term.","iso":"2026-09-21","paper_title":"ITEM 6 Pension Schemes Act 2026 compliance update","paper_url":"https://rbwm.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s73102/73102.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-21","committee":"Berkshire Pension Fund Committee","paper_title":"ITEM 8 App B 2026 ISS draft","paper_url":"https://rbwm.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s73105/73105.pdf","headline":"The Berkshire Pension Fund moved to cash-flow positive at the 2025 valuation, with contributions now exceeding benefit payments.","detail":"The 2025 actuarial valuation found the fund's contributions now exceed pension benefits paid. This is positive news as it means the fund does not require cash injections from the council to pay pensions, and can focus investments on capital growth rather than meeting immediate payment obligations.","category":"income","matters":"A cash-flow positive pension fund reduces the council's immediate financial pressure and risk of unexpected capital calls. This status supports the fund's ability to pursue a long-term investment strategy focused on growth rather than income.","figures":"cash-flow positive status from 2025 valuation","quote":"At the 2025 actuarial valuation, the Fund was cash-flow positive (contribution receipts exceed the value of pension benefits payable)","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-21","committee":"Berkshire Pension Fund Committee","paper_title":"ITEM 8 App B 2026 ISS draft","paper_url":"https://rbwm.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s73105/73105.pdf","headline":"The 2025 valuation shows the Berkshire Pension Fund at 86% funding, unchanged from 2022, with full funding targeted by March 2040.","detail":"Both the 2022 and 2025 triennial valuations found the fund at 86% funded. The fund has confirmed this as its priority and is developing investment strategy to achieve 100% funding by March 2040. This funding level represents a material deficit in the scheme that affects contribution requirements and the council's pension liabilities.","category":"reserves","matters":"A pension fund at 86% funding indicates assets fall significantly short of liabilities. This funding gap directly drives contribution rate pressures on scheme employers and represents a material liability for the council as administering authority.","figures":"86% funding level (both 2022 and 2025 valuations), 100% funding target by March 2040","quote":"both the 2022 and the 2025 triennial valuations showed the Fund at 86% funded, and the Fund has confirmed its priority to be fully funded by March 2040 at the latest","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-21","committee":"Berkshire Pension Fund Committee","paper_title":"ITEM 8 App B 2026 ISS draft","paper_url":"https://rbwm.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s73105/73105.pdf","headline":"Scheme employer contributions face a less than 33% probability of exceeding the 35% threshold set as maximum acceptable.","detail":"The fund has set a red threshold maximum for employer contributions of 35%, with analysis showing less than 33% probability that projected rates will exceed this in the short-term. Contributions at this level represent a material financial demand on scheme employers, including the council as administering authority.","category":"demand","matters":"Pension contribution rates directly impact the council's budget and financial sustainability. The specified risk profile around the 35% threshold indicates material uncertainty about future contribution requirements.","figures":"35% maximum threshold, <33% probability of exceeding","quote":"the Fund has set a maximum (red) threshold for total scheme employer contributions of 35% in the short-term, with the likelihood that the project rates exceed that value of less than 33%","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-21","committee":"Berkshire Pension Fund Committee","paper_title":"Berkshire Pension Board Part I Mintues 010926","paper_url":"https://rbwm.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s73100/73100.pdf","headline":"The Berkshire Pension Fund faces a red-rated risk around workforce resilience and key person dependency, with specialist knowledge concentrated in a small number of officers.","detail":"A combined red-rated risk on workforce capacity and succession planning was created. Jo Thistlewood noted that much specialist knowledge was concentrated in a small number of officers and that further work was required to strengthen succession planning and knowledge sharing. Mitigating actions are underway but a full resilience review and workforce strategy remain in development, with capacity constraints limiting progress.","category":"people","matters":"Loss of key pension fund administration staff could disrupt the council's ability to manage its pension obligations and meet regulatory requirements.","figures":"Red-rated risk; 96% of active scheme members covered by i-Connect system.","quote":"Jo Thistlewood explained that the risk related not to current performance but to ensuring sufficient resilience should key individuals unexpectedly leave or become unavailable. She noted that much specialist knowledge was concentrated within a small number of Officers and that further work was required to strengthen succession planning and knowledge sharing.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-21","committee":"Berkshire Pension Fund Committee","paper_title":"Berkshire Pension Board Part I Mintues 010926","paper_url":"https://rbwm.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s73100/73100.pdf","headline":"Local government reorganisation and the proposed creation of the Ridgeway Authority has been identified as a new red-rated risk to the Berkshire Pension Fund with full implications remaining unclear.","detail":"Jo Thistlewood reported a new red-rated risk relating to the proposed Ridgeway Authority. The reorganisation could result in transfers of scheme members, assets and liabilities between pension funds with significant governance, funding and investment implications. The Chair emphasised early engagement with relevant authorities to identify appropriate solutions.","category":"governance","matters":"Local government restructuring affecting Windsor and Maidenhead could materially alter pension fund governance, the council's obligations and funding arrangements for the council and its scheme members.","figures":"New red-rated risk identified; timeline and scope of reorganisation not finalised.","quote":"Jo Thistlewood also reported the addition of a new red risk relating to local government reorganisation and the proposed creation of the Ridgeway Authority, noting that while the full implications for the Fund remained unclear, the changes could result in the transfer of scheme members, assets and liabilities between pension funds and would have significant governance, funding and investment implications.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-21"},"name":"Windsor & Maidenhead UA","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-21","since_iso":"2026-08-22","distress":false,"headline":"The Berkshire Pension Fund moved to cash-flow positive at the 2025 valuation, with contributions now exceeding benefit payments.","lead":"A cash-flow positive pension fund reduces the council's immediate financial pressure and risk of unexpected capital calls. This status supports the fund's ability to pursue a long-term investment strategy focused on growth rather than income.","also":["8 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Place Overview and Scrutiny Panel on 2026-09-23","n_findings":9,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"ITEM 8 App B 2026 ISS draft","top_paper_url":"https://rbwm.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s73105/73105.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":99,"news_drafts_total":1}}